aracter suit. If I discard W8, it's less likely to be needed by others. The player across has W6, W7, W8, so they already have it. So discarding W8 is safe.\n\nBut if I discard T7, which is in the Bamboo suit, and the player across has T7 in their melds, they already have it. So discarding T7 is also safe.\n\nBetween the two, which is better for my hand? If I discard T7, I can later aim for All Terminals and Honors. If I discard W8, same. But I have two W3s and two W9s, which are needed for potential Pungs. So maybe it's better to keep T7 and discard W8, since W8 is not part of any Pung I'm aiming for. Or vice versa.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should discard a tile that's part of a pair. For example, I have two W9s. If I discard one, I can keep the other as a pair. But if I need a Pung of W9s, I need another one. But if I discard one, it's a pair, which could be part of the winning hand.\n\nBut in the current hand, if I discard W9, the remaining W9 is a single. But if I discard W9, maybe someone can take it for a Pung. Since there are three left, it's possible. But if I keep it, I can use it for a pair or Pung.\n\nHmm. This is getting complicated. Let me try to outline possible options:\n\nOption 1: Discard T7. This removes a non-terminal, helping towards All Terminals and Honors. If I can later discard W8 and W3, I can have a hand with all terminals and honors.\n\nOption 2: Discard W8. Same as above, but removes a different non-terminal.\n\nOption 3: Discard W3. This could allow someone to Peng, but I can still have one W3 left. If I can draw another, I can form a Pung.\n\nOption 4: Discard F2. This is an honor tile. If I discard it, others might take it. But if I keep it, it's part of the honors in All Terminals and Honors.\n\nOption 5: Discard T1. This is a terminal, but if discarded, someone might take it for a Chow. But looking at the melds, no one has T2 or T3 to take it. So it's safe.\n\nBut I need to choose one. Considering safety and future potential, discar