d has one more W1, making four. So that's a kong. So the action BuGang W1 is valid here. But since the unshown tiles have W1:1, there's one left. If I can kong, that would be good for points. But I need to check if I can kong right now. Since I have four W1s, and the meld is a pung, then yes, I can kong. So that's a possible action.\n\nNow, considering the other plays. The other options are to play B9, W9, T1, W1, F4, T9, B1. Let's see. My hand has tiles towards a Seven Orphans? Wait, no. The Thirteen Orphans requires one of each terminal and honor, plus a duplicate. But I don't have all of them. Alternatively, maybe I'm building towards a different hand.\n\nLooking at the melds: two pungs of W1 and W3. So I have two pungs already. The remaining tiles in my hand are W9, T1, T9, B1, B9, F4. Let's see. The F4 is a North Wind. My seat wind is West, so if I have a pung of West Wind, that would be good. But I don't have any F3 or F4 in pungs except the F4 in my hand. Wait, my hand has F4:1. If I can make a pung of F4, that would help. But there are only four F4 tiles? Wait, no. The honor tiles have four of each wind. The unshown tiles show F4:1, meaning one left. So if I have one F4, and there's one left, maybe another player has some. But I can't make a pung unless I get two more.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can focus on completing a hand with all terminals. My current hand has W1, W9, T1, T9, B1, B9. If I can get a pair, that would be All Terminals. Let's see. The All Terminals pattern is worth 64 points. The example is [T1, T1, T1, B1, B1, B1, W9, W9, W9, B9, B9, B9, T9, T9]. So four of each suit's terminals. Wait, but my hand has one of each terminal in three suits. To make All Terminals, I need four of each terminal? No, the example shows three of each terminal. Wait, no, the example is [T1, T1, T1, B1, B1, B1, W9, W9, W9, B9, B9, B9, T9, T9]. That's three of each terminal in each suit. So All Terminals requires that the hand consists of only terminal tiles (1 or 9 of